EXT. HARBOUR SLIPWAY - DAWN

Grey water. A rowing boat lies on its side in the mud, rope trailing. NELL (30s, oilskin, sleepless) walks the length of it, counting the planks under her breath.

TOM (V.O.)
She always counted things when she was frightened.

NELL
(to herself)
Fourteen. There were fifteen.

She crouches. One plank is new: pale, unpainted, nailed in a hurry.

CUT TO:
